1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,760
Every Orchard Core site starts from a recipe.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:07,982
The recipe you choose on the Setup screen decides which features are on,

3
00:00:07,982 --> 00:00:10,850
which theme is active, and what content exists.

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,340
This video compares the starter recipes.

5
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:22,890
A starter recipe is a list of instructions that Orchard Core follows once,

6
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:24,684
when it sets up a site.

7
00:00:24,684 --> 00:00:27,716
It can enable features and activate themes.

8
00:00:27,716 --> 00:00:32,480
It can also create roles, content types such as Blog Post, and content.

9
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:35,698
You choose one recipe on the Setup screen.

10
00:00:35,698 --> 00:00:39,452
It decides how the site starts, not what it can become, because you

11
00:00:39,452 --> 00:00:42,640
can enable more features and change the theme afterward.

12
00:00:43,390 --> 00:00:47,345
Which recipes you see depends on the application that is running.

13
00:00:47,345 --> 00:00:51,523
Blank site and Headless site come with the CMS core, and the standard

14
00:00:51,523 --> 00:00:54,810
CMS application adds a recipe for each starter theme.

15
00:00:59,093 --> 00:01:02,873
This is the Setup screen of a site that has not been set up.

16
00:01:02,873 --> 00:01:07,512
Next to the site name, the Recipe button opens the list of starter recipes.

17
00:01:07,512 --> 00:01:10,203
A separate video covers the other fields.

18
00:01:10,698 --> 00:01:14,087
Each entry has a name and a short description.

19
00:01:14,087 --> 00:01:16,954
The entries are in alphabetical order:

20
00:01:16,954 --> 00:01:22,558
Agency, Blank site, Blog, Coming Soon, Headless site, and Software as a Service.

21
00:01:27,163 --> 00:01:30,521
Software as a Service is selected when the screen opens.

22
00:01:30,521 --> 00:01:31,820
Let's choose Blog.

23
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:37,073
The name on the Recipe button changes, and Finish Setup installs the site with that recipe.

24
00:01:41,273 --> 00:01:46,313
Blank site enables the content management features and activates the admin theme.

25
00:01:46,313 --> 00:01:49,905
It sets no site theme and no home page, so the front end

26
00:01:49,905 --> 00:01:51,353
is yours to design.

27
00:01:52,103 --> 00:01:55,535
Use it when you build your own theme, or when you run a

28
00:01:55,535 --> 00:02:00,710
decoupled site, where developers write the pages and Orchard Core manages the content.

29
00:02:00,710 --> 00:02:04,873
Otherwise, start from another recipe and change the theme afterward.

30
00:02:05,623 --> 00:02:09,779
Headless site is for using Orchard Core as an API as well as

31
00:02:09,779 --> 00:02:11,919
a content management system.

32
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:17,523
It enables the GraphQL and OpenID Connect features, and its home page is the admin.

33
00:02:18,273 --> 00:02:23,825
The recipe also gives the Authenticated role, which every signed-in user has, permissions

34
00:02:23,825 --> 00:02:27,098
that include View all content and Execute GraphQL.

35
00:02:27,098 --> 00:02:31,423
Review them under Access Control, Roles before you publish the site.

36
00:02:35,676 --> 00:02:39,603
Blog activates The Blog Theme and makes the blog the home page.

37
00:02:39,603 --> 00:02:43,359
On a site set up with this recipe, a header shows the blog's

38
00:02:43,359 --> 00:02:46,546
title and description, and the posts follow below.

39
00:02:47,065 --> 00:02:49,612
The recipe creates a first blog post.

40
00:02:49,612 --> 00:02:53,937
Its preview shows a title, a subtitle, the author and the date, and

41
00:02:53,937 --> 00:02:56,425
the category and tags it belongs to.

42
00:02:56,918 --> 00:02:59,558
The main menu links to Home and About.

43
00:02:59,558 --> 00:03:03,998
About is an Article, one of the content types the recipe adds, along

44
00:03:03,998 --> 00:03:06,758
with Blog Post, Page, Tag, and Category.

45
00:03:08,358 --> 00:03:14,279
The Blog Theme also carries optional recipes for SQL, Lucene, and Elasticsearch search.

46
00:03:14,279 --> 00:03:19,054
They are not starter recipes, so the Setup screen does not list them.

47
00:03:19,054 --> 00:03:21,918
You run them later from Tools, Recipes.

48
00:03:26,218 --> 00:03:30,027
Agency activates The Agency Theme and sets up a company website.

49
00:03:30,027 --> 00:03:33,673
The home page is a landing page, with a header that shows the

50
00:03:33,673 --> 00:03:35,958
site name and a Tell Me More button.

51
00:03:36,515 --> 00:03:39,600
The menu links to the sections below the header:

52
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:42,571
Services, Portfolio, About, Team, and Contact.

53
00:03:42,571 --> 00:03:46,914
The recipe fills most of them with sample content, which you change by

54
00:03:46,914 --> 00:03:48,685
editing the landing page.

55
00:03:52,931 --> 00:03:57,579
Coming Soon activates The Coming Soon Theme and makes one landing page for

56
00:03:57,579 --> 00:03:59,439
a site under construction.

57
00:03:59,439 --> 00:04:03,391
It has a heading, a message, an email field, and social icons.

58
00:04:03,918 --> 00:04:07,794
Visitors type an email address and select the Notify Me!

59
00:04:07,794 --> 00:04:08,607
button.

60
00:04:08,607 --> 00:04:11,420
Under the email field, a message reads:

61
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:14,171
ReCaptcha settings are not configured.

62
00:04:14,171 --> 00:04:20,048
It stays until you save a Site Key and a Secret Key under Settings, Security, reCaptcha.

63
00:04:21,648 --> 00:04:27,168
A workflow named User Registration validates the form, registers a user for the

64
00:04:27,168 --> 00:04:30,156
address, and sends a confirmation email.

65
00:04:30,156 --> 00:04:32,884
You find it under Design, Workflows.

66
00:04:32,884 --> 00:04:39,508
The recipe also enables the Email, Forms, ReCaptcha, Workflows, and Users Registration features.

67
00:04:43,808 --> 00:04:49,474
Software as a Service activates The Default Theme, and its home page is a welcome message.

68
00:04:49,474 --> 00:04:54,727
The recipe enables the Tenants feature, which lets you manage several sites, called

69
00:04:54,727 --> 00:04:57,678
tenants, from the admin of one installation.

70
00:04:59,278 --> 00:05:05,083
Under Multi-Tenancy, Tenants, the Add Tenant button opens a form with a Recipe list.

71
00:05:05,083 --> 00:05:09,792
Each tenant can start from a recipe of its own, so one installation

72
00:05:09,792 --> 00:05:12,888
can host a blog, an agency site, and more.

73
00:05:17,088 --> 00:05:20,785
For a site where you design the front end, start with Blank site.

74
00:05:20,785 --> 00:05:25,628
For an application that serves content to other applications, start with Headless site.

75
00:05:26,378 --> 00:05:31,159
For a theme with sample content, pick Blog, Agency, or Coming Soon.

76
00:05:31,159 --> 00:05:36,268
To host several sites from one installation, pick Software as a Service.

77
00:05:37,018 --> 00:05:40,488
A recipe sets the starting point, not the limits.

78
00:05:40,488 --> 00:05:46,291
You enable more features under Tools, Features, change the theme under Design, Themes,

79
00:05:46,291 --> 00:05:49,319
and run more recipes under Tools, Recipes.

80
00:05:49,319 --> 00:05:51,968
Separate videos cover each of these.

81
00:05:53,968 --> 00:05:57,808
Pick the recipe closest to the site you want, then adjust its features

82
00:05:57,808 --> 00:05:59,374
and theme from the admin.

83
00:05:59,374 --> 00:06:00,688
Thanks for watching.

